  "description": "ROSNUK crystallizes in the trigonal crystal system with space group P 31 2 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H64 Gd6 Mo4 N4 O40 2-,2(C4 H12 N1 1+),C1 H4 O1,14(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mo1 (Mo) has 6 O neighbors; Mo2 (Mo) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1E (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3E (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Mo1E (Mo) has 6 O neighbors; Mo2E (Mo) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.337-4.277 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.78-166.81°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (Me4N)2[Gd6Mo4O12(rac-L)4(OOCCH3)8]·CH3OH·14H2O.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
